`hlen` is `unsigned int` (32-bit), `len` is `size_t` (64-bit on 64-bit). `len + hlen` promotes `hlen` to `size_t`, so no overflow.

But wait, `len` comes from `*taglen` which is `size_t`. And in `sc_asn1_read_tag`, `*taglen = len` where `len = a` and `a` is `unsigned int`. So `len` is at most `UINT_MAX`. `hlen` is at most a few bytes (the tag header). So `len + hlen` can't overflow `size_t` on 64-bit.

